+# Social pathway diagnostic
+
+Base: combined ordinary source commit 7a15a2f8ceffb871947ca7df819095d2cab99327, tree 0a34d588488c09f9a7fd4d8bc6115be61bdcd750. This is the local integration of PR303, PR304 and PR305, not a claim about the latest remote ref.
+
+## Default and scope
+CanonicalNewGameConfig::phase3 selects Nano512 and GroundedObjectSlotsV1. Canonical N2048 creation uses explicit candidate APIs. The neural fixture creates actual canonical Nano newborn genomes, then uses N512FounderFoundationProjection::compile, the inherited founder-overlay route. It does not substitute the procedural scaffold or the separate research N2048 DriveBalance factor.
+
+The additive neural test reports directed nonzero recurrent reachability from homeostasis lane 4, reachable decoder weights, direct innate family configuration, and target-specific scores at loneliness 0/.15/.8 for three disposable fixture seeds (41,96001,96002). Peer and toy observations use the same position and physical properties; actual candidate/flat-sensory equality is measured rather than assumed. Ordinary social context is not converted into a privileged target preference.
+
+Fresh_activations and decode are the existing repository CPU diagnostic spelling of compiled encoder/recurrent/candidate arithmetic with zero mutable banks, neutral receptor effects and all routes enabled subject to cadence. Reachability is a graph upper bound, not proof of timed activation. The reported argmax is diagnostic score ranking, not a sampled factorized motor policy, trained behavior, actual GPU execution or an autonomous life. No chemistry or learned state is overwritten: need perturbations apply to disposable perception frames only.
+
+The additive world fixture uses canonical living founders after 600 ordinary development ticks and compares continuous contact, separation, and 20 intervals of contact followed by separation, through 100 further ordinary world ticks. It checks relative drive ordering and one matching biology tick and logs concentrations at predefined points. Existing contact tests supply dose/collision/dead-body/save/rollback coverage. No new seed cohort or autonomous learning is run.
+
+## Execution
+Runner: ../run-social-pathway-diagnostic-v1.sh. This must run only after the shared-target owner's release. Output: ../social-pathway-diagnostic-v1.log. At preparation time, execution is pending target scheduling. No outcome is claimed yet.
+
+## Change decision
+No neural or chemical candidate has yet been implemented. If the default route is disconnected, a candidate must be identity-bound and separately controlled. If peer identity cannot affect the available neural/candidate features, increasing generic Contact salience would not demonstrate social targeting. Do not add a hidden target label or raise loneliness pressure to hide that representation gap.
+
+## App caller verification
+`NewGameFounderSelection` in `crates/alife_game_app/src/new_game_lifecycle.rs` derives default `BuiltinNano512`; `stage_phase3_new_game` and `create_canonical_new_game_runtime` pass this default. `production_voxel_frontend.rs` launch defaults also use it. The N2048 override occurs only under explicit `N2048Candidate { asset_path }`, while explicit `ScaledChoiceNociceptiveV1` remains Nano but is a distinct recipe. This establishes the pinned source's unconfigured New Game default, not the user's actual selected launch flags or class of a loaded creature.
+
+The diagnostic inventory now covers all eleven drive lanes for each default Nano founder: hunger, fatigue, fear, pain, loneliness, curiosity, brain ATP, temperature stress, reproductive drive, and extension lanes 9/10. It distinguishes all structural recurrent paths from nonzero-weight paths and prints direct innate masks separately. These are conservative reachability upper bounds, not effective modulation or successful action selection. Only loneliness has matched causal score perturbations in this fixture.
+
+## Measured results
+The first compile found a fixture enum typo (`Toy` instead of `ActivityToy`), fixed before execution; failure log is preserved separately. The completed run passed the two new diagnostics and the existing contact suite (8 passed, 1 existing ignored; new time-series test is included in that suite). Full founder regression file passed 8/8. Strict world all-target Clippy, workspace fmt and diff checks passed. Logs: ../social-pathway-diagnostic-v1.log and ../social-pathway-checks-v1.log. Machine-readable inventory: ../social-pathway-summary-v1.json.
+
+All eleven default Nano lanes encode in three founder overlays. None reaches a candidate decoder through structural or nonzero compiled recurrent paths. Hunger reaches the reserve/homeostasis region; other drive input nodes have no recurrent exits. Direct innate family masks separately cover hunger, fatigue, fear, pain and temperature. This does not imply absent ATP/sleep/body regulation or rule out acquired lifetime structural paths.
+
+In 108 detached matched score cases (three founders, peer/non-peer, three loneliness levels, six sequence lengths), the 72 need perturbation comparisons all had exactly zero candidate-score differences. Activations and metabolic state persist through each fixed-context sequence; tested lengths 1/2/4/8/16/32 frames equal 4/8/16/32/64/128 microsteps. Loneliness does change its neural activity, but not readout. All cases retain their diagnostic argmax; this is not a sampled motor bundle or learned policy. Actual peer and equally physical toy have equal candidate and flat sensory features here, with observed peer context present only for the peer.
+
+Native body chemistry works: from developed loneliness .15, 20 contact intervals reduce it to .0453754; continued contact reaches zero by interval40. Separation after20 returns it to .146007 by interval100 while continuous contact remains zero. This proves recurrent bounded need and real satiation in these fixtures, not emotional experience.
+
+## Next factor
+No existing default is changed. Parent requested a separate explicitly identified fresh Nano drive-routing candidate, with unchanged and equal-budget/zero-bridge controls, after checking birth dendrites and acquired target-context memory. Existing motor-only birth dendrites do not bridge drive inputs. Lifetime structural growth can potentially create new paths, so no universal impossibility claim is warranted. Existing tracked-target memory may support consequence-based social preference without a hidden peer label; that path must be preserved and measured separately.
